    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186166867,
      "id": "53a1649d-4279-5b7c-839c-728f333b2c3f",
      "title": "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parabola"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a1aa4ef3-4039-5b42-9641-e3c2240ca725",
      ":question/problem": "![](/tmp/course-academy-g2-readonly-tly0pcma/17592186166867/caller-easy/generated/523b07a7ed091dd4e3b53ebd65abf5b679e4c7ced4d56198e661855a7e37c686.png)\n\nThe parabola shown above has equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=49x.\n$$\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "7e20a56e-021c-5745-966e-05e5c646896e",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "f2364893-d8b9-5174-aa01-512eec38bfea",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{49}{2y}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "6e32a3d0-9438-57fb-8b2b-56043805c262",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{2y}{49}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "f8dcff5c-c214-53a6-8f6a-d7fc177f8793",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{49}{y}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "aeed9a8f-4f5f-5926-af21-4075200c4983",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{49}{2}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "9745bf86-dd9e-531a-82cb-aad2c46962ff",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{49}{2y}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "f2364893-d8b9-5174-aa01-512eec38bfea"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "The equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=49x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(49x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =49 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{49}{2y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy"
    },
