    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "de9db8a3-4708-5ef4-b950-debdb33647c6",
      ":question/problem": "![](/tmp/course-academy-g2-readonly-tly0pcma/17592186166867/caller-easy/generated/c8d4c5d02a2d26990b4fcca522ec9df6901cfe13350784e9c7dd54181e033f19.png)\n\nThe parabola shown above has equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4x.\n$$\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b107d6d3-7523-5256-becb-c303d326d89a",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "b81278c9-1630-5384-ab82-2be49b854df6",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{2}{y}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "b81278c9-1630-5384-ab82-2be49b854df6"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "The equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy"
    },
